{"type":"message","id":"41a1e93f","parentId":"e0c7c623","timestamp":"2026-02-02T00:19:46.195Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a live Mission Control dashboard at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/mission-control/\n\nThis is a real-time ambient display designed to run 24/7 on a monitor. Dark theme, auto-refreshing, glanceable from across the room.\n\n## Architecture\n- Single index.html with inline CSS/JS (self-contained)\n- Fetches data from the existing Bureh API at localhost:3002 (already has /api/health, /api/status, /api/investments, /api/costs, /api/links, /api/medtech endpoints)\n- Also fetches directly from some data files via a small Express server\n- Auto-refreshes every 10 seconds\n\n## Create: server.js\nSimple Express server on port 3100 (replace lebbie-chocolates which is on 3100 — actually use port 3200):\n- Serves static index.html\n- API endpoints:\n  - GET /api/activity — reads last 20 lines from PM2 logs (parse pm2 jlist + recent log lines)\n  - GET /api/polymarket — reads /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/polymarket-copytrade/data/strategy-state.json\n  - GET /api/scout — reads latest scout report from /home/ec2-user/clawd/agents/scout/reports/ (most recent .md file)\n  - GET /api/medtech — reads from biomed-borbor health endpoint (proxy localhost:3000/health) + DB stats\n  - GET /api/system — system stats (CPU, RAM, disk, uptime) via execSync\n  - GET /api/processes — pm2 jlist parsed\n  - GET /api/costs — proxy from localhost:3002/api/costs\n  - GET /api/investments — proxy from localhost:3002/api/investments\n\n## Create: index.html (THE MAIN BUILD)\n\n### Design Requirements:\n- **Dark theme** — near-black background (#0a0a0f), with glowing accents\n- **Color palette**: \n  - Background: #0a0a0f\n  - Cards: #12121a with subtle border glow\n  - Primary text: #e0e0e0\n  - Secondary text: #888\n  - Green: #00ff88 (healthy/positive)\n  - Red: #ff4444 (alerts/negative)\n  - Blue: #4488ff (info)\n  - Gold: #ffaa00 (warnings)\n  - Purple: #aa66ff (accent)\n- **Font**: 'JetBrains Mono' for data, 'Inter' for labels (Google Fonts)\n- **No scrolling needed** — everything fits on one screen (optimize for 1080p and 4K)\n- **Subtle animations**: pulse on live data, fade transitions on updates, gentle glow effects\n- **Auto-refresh**: every 10 seconds, smooth transitions (no flicker/flash)\n\n### Layout (CSS Grid, 6 panels):\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  🧠 BAI BUREH — MISSION CONTROL              Live • 🟢 │\n├───────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│                       │                                 │\n│   LIVE ACTIVITY FEED  │    PROCESSES                    │\n│   (scrolling ticker)  │    (PM2 status grid)            │\n│                       │                                 │\n├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│                       │                                 │\n│   POLYMARKET          │    SCOUT INTEL                  │\n│   (6 strategies)      │    (latest findings)            │\n│                       │                                 │\n├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│                       │                                 │\n│   BIOMED BORBOR       │    SYSTEM HEALTH                │\n│   (stats + last msg)  │    (CPU/RAM/Disk/Cost/Uptime)   │\n│                       │                                 │\n└───────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Panel 1: LIVE ACTIVITY FEED (top-left)\n- Scrolling feed of recent activity, newest at top\n- Each entry: timestamp + icon + description\n- Sources: PM2 logs, file changes, messages\n- Examples:\n  - \"23:42 📤 Sent message to Doug on Telegram\"\n  - \"23:40 🔧 Sub-agent completed: borbor-data-fix\"\n  - \"23:35 📊 Polymarket scan #2100: 0 opportunities\"\n  - \"23:30 💓 Heartbeat: OK\"\n- Max 8-10 visible entries, auto-scrolls\n- New entries fade in from top with green glow\n\n### Panel 2: PROCESSES (top-right)\n- Grid of PM2 processes\n- Each process: name + status dot (🟢 online, 🔴 stopped, 🟡 errored)\n- Show: uptime, restarts, memory\n- Compact grid layout, 2-3 columns\n- Pulsing green dot for healthy processes\n\n### Panel 3: POLYMARKET STRATEGIES (mid-left)\n- 6 strategy cards in a mini-grid (2x3 or 3x2)\n- Each card shows:\n  - Strategy name\n  - Capital remaining\n  - P&L (colored green/red)\n  - Open positions count\n  - Win rate\n- Color the entire card border based on performance (green = profit, red = loss, gray = inactive)\n\n### Panel 4: SCOUT INTEL (mid-right)  \n- Latest scan summary\n- Count of threats 🔴, watches 🟡, opportunities 🟢\n- Top 3 most important findings (1-line each)\n- \"Last scan: X hours ago\" + \"Next: 6:00 AM ET\"\n- JOC leads count if available\n\n### Panel 5: BIOMED BORBOR (bottom-left)\n- Stats: technicians registered, total issues, resolved issues\n- Last message timestamp\n- WhatsApp status (connected/disconnected)\n- Resolution rate percentage with progress bar\n\n### Panel 6: SYSTEM HEALTH (bottom-right)\n- CPU usage (bar or gauge)\n- RAM usage (bar or gauge)  \n- Disk usage (bar or gauge)\n- Server uptime\n- Today's API cost\n- Investment prices (Silver, GSVRF) if available from /api/investments\n\n### Header Bar:\n- \"🧠 BAI BUREH — MISSION CONTROL\" on left\n- Current date/time (updates every second) on right\n- \"Live\" indicator with pulsing green dot\n- Subtle gradient line underneath\n\n### Footer Bar (optional):\n- Scrolling ticker with latest Scout findings or Polymarket updates\n\n## PM2 Setup:\n- Add to ecosystem or start directly\n- Process name: mission-control\n- Port: 3200\n- Start cloudflared tunnel: mission-tunnel on port 3200\n\n## IMPORTANT:\n- Must work WITHOUT the Bureh API if it's down (graceful degradation — show \"unavailable\" per panel)\n- All fetches use try/catch with timeout\n- No external dependencies except express (npm init, npm install express)\n- Google Fonts loaded via CDN\n- Must look GORGEOUS — this is meant to impress. Think sci-fi command center, not boring dashboard.\n- Test that it starts and serves correctly\n- Stop lebbie-chocolates PM2 process if it conflicts (it's on 3100, we're on 3200 so should be fine)\n\nAfter building, start via PM2 + tunnel, verify it loads, and output the public URL."}],"timestamp":1769991586194}}
